{"id": "tea:asokan-edicts:pe7", "source": "src:asokan-edicts", "location": {"ref": "pe7"}, "paraphrase": "The dhamma-mahāmātras are appointed to the affairs of the Saṅgha, of the brāhmaṇas, of the Ājīvikas, of the Nigaṇṭhas, and of the various other sects.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "ethical-social", "naya": null, "path": ["general"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["teacher-transmission"], "speaker": "Aśoka", "teachers": ["tch:asoka"], "notes": "Pillar Edict 7 (Delhi–Topra); from memory.", "coverage": ["B1"], "reported_by_opponent": false, "ai_translated": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U33-sramana"], "disagreements": []}, "correction_log": [], "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U33-sramana"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:asokan-edicts:re12", "source": "src:asokan-edicts", "location": {"ref": "re12"}, "paraphrase": "The king honours all sects, ascetics and householders alike, with gifts and honours, but values most the growth of their essentials; its root is restraint of speech — not praising one's own sect or disparaging another's without cause; one who praises his own sect out of devotion harms it; concord (samavāya) is good, that all may hear and follow one another's dharma.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "ethical-social", "naya": null, "path": ["general"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["ethics"], "speaker": "Aśoka (Piyadasi)", "concepts": ["cpt:sramana-brahmana-contrast"], "teachers": ["tch:asoka"], "notes": "Rock Edict 12 (Girnār/Shāhbāzgarhī versions); paraphrase from memory of standard translations.", "coverage": ["B1"], "reported_by_opponent": false, "ai_translated": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U33-sramana"], "disagreements": []}, "correction_log": [], "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U33-sramana"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
{"id": "tea:asokan-edicts:re13", "source": "src:asokan-edicts", "location": {"ref": "re13"}, "paraphrase": "There is no land, except among the Greeks, where these orders — brāhmaṇas and śramaṇas — are not found, and none where people do not hold to some sect.", "tags": {"level": "conventional", "standpoint": "ethical-social", "naya": null, "path": ["general"], "stage": "all"}, "types": ["teacher-transmission"], "speaker": "Aśoka", "terms": ["trm:sramana"], "concepts": ["cpt:sramana-brahmana-contrast"], "teachers": ["tch:asoka"], "notes": "Rock Edict 13; from memory.", "coverage": ["B1"], "reported_by_opponent": false, "ai_translated": false, "fidelity": {"status": "unchecked"}, "extraction": {"method": "skeleton", "extractors": ["U33-sramana"], "disagreements": []}, "correction_log": [], "verification": {"level": "skeleton", "confidence": "moderate", "unverified": false, "checks": []}, "provenance": {"units": ["skeleton:U33-sramana"], "phases": ["skeleton"]}}
